{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "If Statements in Java"}, {"type": "position", "content": 9}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 2}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.1"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear in Java."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Talk about important information about client software for the identity metasystem  Describe a general-purpose computer programming language   Talk about principles, concepts, characteristics of general-purpose computer programming language "}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.  Exchanges simple information on principles, concepts, and features of general purpose computer programming languages."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe7n5le02ob09re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Should for what is advisable."}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Should is used for mild obligation and advice."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class =\u201ditalic\u201d>Should is an auxiliary verb used to give advice or recommendation and mild obligation. It is also used to say that something is a good idea. <br><br> </span><strong>Form:</strong> <span class =\u201ditalic\u201d>should+ base form of the verb  </br> <i>You<strong> should read more</strong> about the\u201cif statements\u201d. </i><br><br> Should is followed by a verb in the base form and not by a <i>to infinitive.</i><br> <s>You should to use fork to run more than one process.</s><br><br> <strong>Should,</strong> as any modal verb, doesn't agree with the subject in time and person."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I think you should give me an example of a Java \u201cif\u201d statement."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You should give me a quick review of what an \u201cif\u201d statement is."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Superlative"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Superlatives are the form of an adjective that indicates it has the greatest quality. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class =\u201ditalic\u201d>Use superlative adjectives when you want to compare 3 or more nouns to the highest degree.  <br> Generally, when the adjective has one syllable we add the <strong> \u2013est </strong> ending to form a superlative. </br>  e.g. clean-clean<strong>est</strong> <br><br> If there is a vowel followed by a consonant at the end of the adjective, we double the last consonant. <br> e.g. hot- hot<strong>test</strong> <br><br> If the adjective ends in <strong>\u2013y</strong> , we change it to <strong>i</strong> <br>  e.g. happy- happ<strong>iest</strong><br><br> Exceptions: Some superlatives that are formed using <strong> the most</strong>: <br> <strong>Fun</strong>- the most fun (not funnest) <br><strong> Real</strong> \u2013 the most real (not realest)<br> <strong>Right</strong> \u2013 the most right (not rightest)<br><strong>wrong</strong>\u2013 the most wrong (not wrongest)<br><br> Some adjectives can take the <strong>-est ending </strong>or be formed with <strong> the most</strong>. <br><br> <strong>Clever </strong>- the most clever, the cleverest <br>  <strong>Simple </strong>- the most simple, the simplest<br>  </br> </br>  Adjectives with more than two syllables take <strong>the most</strong>.<br>  </br> Beautiful- <strong>the most </strong>beautiful <br>Interesting- <strong>the most</strong>  interesting<br>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "The \u201cif statement\u201d is one of the most used Boolean expressions."}, {"type": "example", "content": "This is one of the most difficult topics."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "review"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a summary "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You should give me a quick review of what an \u201cif\u201d statement is. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n5le02ob09aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "conditional statement "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a condition that is stated in an expression "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  They have one or more conditional statements to be evaluated and they go along a conditional outcome."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n5le02ob09aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "evaluate "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to test an expression "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: They have one or more conditional statements to be evaluated and they go along a conditional outcome."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n5le02ob09aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "go along with "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to go together with another thing. "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: They have one or more conditional statements to be evaluated and they go along a conditional outcome."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n5le02ob09aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": " determine "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to conclude after observation or examination "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  The \"if-statement\" will be executed when the condition is determined to be true."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n5le02ob09aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Look for information about the if/else statement syntax examples. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write notes and make a chart where you describe many examples of the \u201cif statements\u201d. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read aloud the examples and share with your partner."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I look for information about the if/else statement syntax examples. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I design chart where you describe many examples of the \u201cif statements\u201d. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I talk about the \u201cif statement\u201d examples and its usages. "}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "welcome", "id": 0, "contents": [{}]}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"time": "0", "image": "enpe7n5le02ob09re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<strong>John:</strong> <span class =\u201ditalic\u201d>Hey, Cat! How's it going? Thank you so much for your help last time, you really helped me a lot. We should study together for the next test!</span><br>\n<strong>Catherine:</strong> <span class =\u201ditalic\u201d> Sure! Why not? Have you started reading the newly assigned books? </span><br>\n<strong>John:</strong> <span class =\u201ditalic\u201d>What new books?</span><br>\n<strong>Catherine:</strong> <span class =\u201ditalic\u201d> The ones about the<i>if statements</i>. You should study more! This is one of the most difficult topics!</span><br>"}, {"time": "23900", "image": "enpe7n5le02ob09re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<strong>John:</strong> <span class =\u201ditalic\u201d> You should give me a quick review of what an<i> if statement</i> is. </span><br>\n<strong>Catherine:</strong> <span class =\u201ditalic\u201d> The <i> if statement</i> is one of the most used Boolean expressions. The<i> if statement</i> and the <i>if/else statement</i> can also be called <i>forks</i> or decision making statements. They have one or more conditional statements to be evaluated, and they go along a conditional outcome. The<i> if statement</i> will be executed when the condition is determined to be true,  and the if-else statement will be executed when the condition is false.\n</span><br>\n<strong>John:</strong> <span class =\u201ditalic\u201d>Okay, I see. I think you should give me an example of a Java <i>if statement</i>. </span><br>"}, {"time": "66000", "image": "enpe7n5le02ob09re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<strong>Catherine:</strong> <span class =\u201ditalic\u201d> Sure, this is the most common example. Imagine we can change the color of the page by entering a numerical value. Java has to make the background of the page red if the value I enter is smaller than 5. </span><br>\n<strong>John:</strong> <span class =\u201ditalic\u201d>Okay, can you tell me what happens when an <i>if/else statement</i> is executed? </span><br>\n<strong>Catherine:</strong> <span class =\u201ditalic\u201d> Well, in the <i>if/else statement</i> there are two conditional situations. The first one is when the value is evaluated as \u201ctrue\u201d, and the second one, when it is evaluated as <i>false</i> in which the <i>else</i> part is executed. So, to continue with our previous example: if I enter something bigger than 5 the <i>if/else statement</i> will be executed, making the background blue instead."}], "coverimg": "enpe7n5le02ob09re2img01.jpg", "audiosrc": "enpe7n5le02ob09re2aud01"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "type": "audio", "_data": [], "id": 1, "title": ""}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can explain what the Java if statement is."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can exchange information about examples of if statements in Java. "}, {"type": "Learning Out